1) AI models dont remember conversations

This is probably the biggest misconception among beginners.
Many people think chatgpt or any other AI model automatically remembers everything.
It doesn't. Every request is independent unless you, the developer send the previous conversation along with the new message.

2) Memory lives in the application

The memory was not created inside the AI model
It was created inside our python program.
Our application stored the conversation in a list and sent that list wit every request.
The AI model simply used the information we provided.

3) Python lists are perfect for conversation history

we used one simple list : 
messages = []
Every time someone spoke, we added another message. Nothing more
Some times the simplest solution is also the best one.

4) Every message has two parts

Each message contains : 
{
    "role" : "..",
    "content" : ".."
}
The role tells the model who is speaking
The content tells the model what was said
The simple structure is used by almost every modern conversational AI framework

5) Context creates Intelligence

The AI did not suddenly become smarter overnight
It became more useful because it had more context
Context gives the idea of awarness what the user is trying to ask and it will answer our questions.


So Basically Day2 is a Memory Enabled AI Assistant
